Bind the user-controlled ID as a parameter rather than interpolating it into SQL. Adjust the table and selected columns to match the application schema.
```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

function findUser(PDO $pdo, int $userId): ?array
{
    $statement = $pdo->prepare(
        'SELECT id, name, email FROM users WHERE id = :id'
    );
    $statement->execute(['id' => $userId]);
    $user = $statement->fetch(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);

    return $user === false ? null : $user;
}
```
Configure PDO to use exceptions and disable emulated prepares where supported by the driver.

Authorize before writing data, validate only the accepted fields, then pass that validated data to the model. This assumes a Product policy and fillable fields are configured; adapt the authorization ability and schema to the application.
```php
<?php

namespace App\Http\Controllers;

use App\Models\Product;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Gate;
use Illuminate\Http\JsonResponse;
use Illuminate\Http\Request;

final class ProductController
{
    public function store(Request $request): JsonResponse
    {
        Gate::authorize('create', Product::class);

        $validated = $request->validate([
            'name' => ['required', 'string', 'max:120'],
            'price' => ['required', 'numeric', 'min:0'],
        ]);

        $product = Product::create($validated);

        return response()->json(['data' => $product], 201);
    }
}
```

Keep the test independent of a particular mocking library by describing the collaborator contract. Replace `UserRepository` with the application's actual interface and configure its mock using the PHPUnit version in the project.
```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

use PHPUnit\Framework\TestCase;

final class FindUserTest extends TestCase
{
    public function testReturnsNullWhenUserDoesNotExist(): void
    {
        $repository = $this->createMock(UserRepository::class);
        $repository->expects(self::once())
            ->method('findById')
            ->with(42)
            ->willReturn(null);

        self::assertNull(findUserFromRepository($repository, 42));
    }

    public function testReturnsFoundUser(): void
    {
        $user = ['id' => 42, 'name' => 'Ada'];
        $repository = $this->createMock(UserRepository::class);
        $repository->expects(self::once())
            ->method('findById')
            ->with(42)
            ->willReturn($user);

        self::assertSame($user, findUserFromRepository($repository, 42));
    }
}
```
The examples assume `UserRepository::findById()` and `findUserFromRepository()` exist; adapt names and return types to the codebase.
